+# Room16 joint structural prototype — CPU handoff
+
+This is a local, unaccepted prototype based on `df33589715e11cdec881d00f69a7ca01cf66a1bf`. The existing PR81 worktree/branch is unchanged. No renderer, native capture, publication or merge was performed. Earlier Room16 visual rejections remain valid evidence; these tests do not establish a biological appearance or readable consumed cabinet.
+
+## Concrete change
+
+The closed organ body now has seven corresponding 150-point rings: original outline at heights 0 and 2; inset 3 at 8; inset 7 at 18; inset 3 at 26; original outline at 30.2 and 31. Its top uses the production height function. Two global shared-edge midpoint refinements keep cap/wall seams indexed together. The previously proposed return at 30.8 was rejected: it would leave a physical inset at the 30.4 shot plane. The actual implementation returns at 30.2, and 450 short boundary rays test the complete 30.4 silhouette both before and after production bake.
+
+The cabinet is jointly rebuilt, centered at (684,234), rotated −30 degrees, with an 80×30 enclosure extending from ground to height 39, a connected front, three actual sockets/cores, roof service panel and three buses, two fasteners and a connected jagged lid. One broad organic corner intersects the bed, housing and roof region. The three earlier applied fold/wrap/shoulder pieces are removed. Their count is not an acceptance invariant. Vent slots are deliberately removed in this enclosure redesign; the ports, exposed panel, roof buses and fasteners are the replacement readable hardware roles. The rotated scute clearance mask includes a shallow front apron to expose the actual front faces along the native camera direction.
+
+The exact 150-point gameplay contour, routes, anchors, navigation, camera, input, resources, materials, terminal shapes and cavity geometry are unchanged. The root height cap remains 44.8. All existing non-cabinet terminal/cavity exposure witnesses remain, including the 25-point west tissue patch, three cut crests and east/south tissue. There are still seven materials and the original production bake/disposal checks.
+
+## Explicit old → new assertion map
+
+| Old construction-specific assertion | Replacement / retained invariant |
+| --- | --- |
+| 20 layered meshes: 8 scutes + 9 terminal parts + 3 cabinet folds | 18: the same 8+9 plus one substantial consuming corner; closed manifold, opposite edges and positive volumes remain checked for all pieces. |
+| Organ bottom/top are the first/second half of its vertex buffer | Sectioned body top/bottom classified by actual heights and checked for outward normals; all-edge pairing, nonzero faces, positive volume and corruption controls retained. Other shell half-layout checks unchanged. |
+| Shoulder first hits at (706,230), (710,236), (714,242), old housing overlap at x700 | Nine distributed local points u15/20/25 × v−4/0/4 require actual bed, housing and corner intersections, corner above housing and native first-hit corner. Corner extends to ground. |
+| Old side-wrap and old three port coordinates | 27 first-hit core samples across all three new ports; nine inter-port panel samples. Original east/south tissue rays retained verbatim. |
+| Axis-aligned old housing/front/lid AABB contacts | Inverse-rotated local bounds of actual vertices require positive housing/front and housing/lid overlap, exact front/panel contact, three socket/core overlaps, roof/housing contact and two fastener/housing contact patches. No rotated world-AABB proxy. |
+| Old vent/fastener contact loop | Vent slots deliberately absent; two retained fasteners receive explicit local-space contact assertions. Three sockets, three cores and three roof buses preserve substantive hardware roles. |
+| Single old housing/lid/roof visible coordinates and panel center fallback accepting a port | Distributed direct native first hits: nine roof samples, three lid samples, nine inter-port panel samples and 27 core samples. The panel checks require the panel itself. |
+| Roof area >500 and old fold above housing; old roof bus contacts | New actual local roof area >559, exact roof/housing and bus/roof contacts; nine broad consuming-corner native hits plus actual bed/housing/corner overlap. |
+| Old terminal top, side and attachment rays in mixed cabinet tests | All terminal coordinates, directions, named first hits and actual bed attachment checks retained; only cabinet-specific branches replaced above. |
+| Existing five sampled scute support points | Retained, plus every scute bottom vertex is now ray-checked against the actual refined body. Five probes per vertex retain a 0.0001-game-unit Float32 boundary tolerance. |
+
+The unchanged dense 10-unit ray grids, all solid-vertex/triangle containment, routes at radii 16/28/38, historical topology changes, other-room template identity, fallback-height shots, height/material budgets, gantry gap and three retirement cycles remain in `SwarmJunction.test.ts`.
+
+## Preserved failures and corrections
+
+- `original-tests-red.log`: 7 failures / 34 passes immediately after the joint construction change, preserving obsolete old cabinet coordinates/names and body indexing expectations before replacement.
+- `replacement-exposure-red.log`: the new front patch genuinely hit `carapace-scute-east-inner` instead of core −19/34.5. The rotated front apron was widened in geometry; the exposure assertions were retained and then passed.
+- `float32-support-red.log`: exact shared-boundary ray missed at (397.2766418457,121.4704742432). Support probes now retain the center plus four offsets of only 0.0001 game units, explicitly bounding Float32 rounding tolerance rather than dropping the vertex.
+- `support-budget-red.log`: every-vertex support case took 38 seconds and exceeded the unchanged 5-second test timeout; 46 other cases passed. It is partitioned into 8 scutes × 4 disjoint vertex-index residues. Every original vertex and all five original probes remain. The aggregate >100 support-vertex guard remains. No timeout increase or coverage reduction.
+
+## Verification and timing
+
+Commands run in this worktree:
+
+```
+npx vitest run src/render/sectionedOrganicShell.test.ts src/render/SwarmEmbeddedDistributor.test.ts src/render/SwarmJunction.test.ts src/render/organicShell.test.ts
+npx vitest run src/render/SwarmEmbeddedDistributor.test.ts
+npx tsc --noEmit
+```
+
+The four-file run passed 78 cases (`focused-green.log`, 34.47 seconds total). The subsequent three-case cabinet run passed after adding explicit retained fastener contacts (`fastener-green.log`); typecheck passed. No other source changes followed those checks.
+
+`construction-timing.json` records 12 full model constructions per root (first two excluded from warm summary), with dispose after each. Old df335 warm median 122.64ms, max 203.62ms; prototype warm median 105.68ms, max 234.57ms. These are noisy shared-host CPU observations, not a speedup or frame-time claim. The new body has 16,770 vertices / 33,536 triangles versus 10,674 / 21,344 previously. Input validation and ring correspondence are repeated at construction, not per frame; no caching is introduced. Native loading/readiness, draw cost and visual quality remain unverified. Reproducible timing runner is `/workspace/room16-structural-construction-timing.mjs`.
+
+## Remaining gates and risks
+
+Parent independent diff/test review and a matched native preview are required before acceptance. The concave undercut must read as grounded tissue, not a walkable void or floating slab, and the larger enclosure must read as consumed machinery rather than a perched cap. CPU geometry alone cannot answer either question. Full repository/browser `npm run verify` has not run for this prototype because this task explicitly forbids GPU/renderer execution; focused CPU/typecheck results are not a substitute. The helper validates its supported rings and rejects sharp/invalid inset configurations; it is not a general arbitrary-polygon offset engine.
